le in `v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]`, `v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbd]`, `v4.6.rc1.official [481f36ed2]`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable unknown - EndeavourOS #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 11 Jan 2026 17:10:53 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Mesa Intel(R) UHD Graphics 630 (CFL GT2) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-9750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 31.13 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm creating a controller input display application. When holding down a button on the joypad and switching window focus, `Input.is_joy_button_pressed` is returning false despite the button still being pressed on the joypad.\n\nFrom the following video below, observe how `jstest-gtk` is correctly showing buttons pressed but Godot is not (look at the \"Pressed: \" text and the colors on the display - blue means pressed).\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/401ed936-3b1e-4084-a832-35433e894b36\n\nThe issue is present on X11 and in exported builds.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Use `Input.is_joy_button_pressed` in a script\n2. Hold down at least one button on a game controller\n3. Change window focus\n4. Observe how all the acknowledged button inputs are dropped by Godot\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[GodotBugReproProject.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24698424/GodotBugReproProject.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo